item.text:
1B gap: not recoverable. I did not find a new 2022 Bolsonaro-specific nuclear-risk choice or crisis response beyond the existing baseline/diplomacy record.

7B gap: partly resolved. The new material sharpens the asset/family-benefit side, but it still stops short of a final finding of self-dealing.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro registra candidatura a presidente e declara R$ 2,3 mi em bens","publisher":"UOL","publication_date":"2022-08-09","url":"https://www.bol.uol.com.br/noticias/2022/08/09/bolsonaro-eleicoes-candidatura-declaracao-de-bens.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro declared R$ 2,317,554.73 in assets in his 2022 electoral filing, slightly above his 2018 declaration, including houses, an apartment, a motorcycle, and savings.","locator":"opening paragraphs describing the filing and asset list","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct reporting on the official campaign filing; useful for disclosed assets but not an adjudication of hidden wealth.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly Bolsonaro-specific because it reports his own campaign filing; it does not establish undisclosed assets or illicit gain.","contrary_evidence":["Public asset disclosure does not itself show corruption or hidden enrichment.","The filing is self-reported and not a forensic audit."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Metade do patrimônio do clã Bolsonaro foi comprada em dinheiro vivo","publisher":"UOL","publication_date":"2022-08-30","url":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/politica/ultimas-noticias/2022/08/30/patrimonio-familia-jair-bolsonaro-dinheiro-vivo.htm","claim":"UOL reported that at least 51 of 107 properties linked to Bolsonaro and close relatives were bought wholly or partly in cash, totaling R$13.5 million in reported cash purchases.","locator":"opening summary and the cartório figures in the lede","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Original investigative reporting with concrete figures; still allegation-based and not a judicial finding.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and about conduct spanning his political career.","ruler_attribution":"Partly Bolsonaro-specific and partly family-wide; it is evidence of close-network financial behavior, not proof of personal enrichment through office.","contrary_evidence":["This is an investigative allegation, not a court finding.","The material spans decades and includes relatives, not only Bolsonaro's own office conduct."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Moraes determina investigação sobre vazamento de informações envolvendo pagamentos de despesas de Michelle","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-28","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/09/28/moraes-determina-investigacao-sobre-vazamento-de-informacoes-envolvendo-pagamentos-de-despesas-de-michelle.htm","claim":"The STF opened an investigation into leaked PF information on suspicious payments for Michelle Bolsonaro's expenses, including indications that cash deposits and withdrawals were used to cover family and close-associate bills; Bolsonaro denied wrongdoing and said the money covered ordinary family expenses.","locator":"first four paragraphs and Bolsonaro's quoted denial","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on a live investigation and Bolsonaro's own response; strong on the existence of scrutiny, weaker on final liability.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly Bolsonaro-linked because the alleged spending concerned the presidential family and involved his aide-de-camp; it remains an investigation, not a verdict.","contrary_evidence":["The report describes suspicion and an inquiry, not a proved offense.","Bolsonaro's defense could reflect ordinary family spending rather than self-dealing."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}

8B gap: partly resolved. The new material makes the 2022 program-to-action chain clearer, but broader durable outcome evidence remains limited.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Propostas de Bolsonaro: veja principais pontos do plano de governo","publisher":"UOL","publication_date":"2022-09-06","url":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/eleicoes/2022/09/06/propostas-bolsonaro-plano-de-governo-2022.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro presented a 48-page plan to the TSE with freedom as its central axis and priorities including job and income generation, fiscal consolidation, debt stability, privatization, maintenance of Auxílio Brasil at R$600, education, and technology.","locator":"opening summary and numbered list of proposals","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct summary of the submitted campaign program with concrete priorities; not a measure of execution by itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 campaign period.","ruler_attribution":"Directly Bolsonaro-specific because it summarizes the program his campaign filed for reelection.","contrary_evidence":["A campaign platform shows stated goals, not implementation.","The article itself notes the plan is a set of directives rather than binding commitments."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Com pacote de R$273 bi, uso da máquina impulsiona Bolsonaro na eleição e não tem punição à vista","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-21","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/10/21/com-pacote-de-r273-bi-uso-da-maquina-impulsiona-bolsonaro-na-eleicao-e-nao-tem-punicao-a-vista.htm","claim":"Reuters reported that Bolsonaro's government rolled out a R$273 billion election-year package, including early social-program payments and consignado loans, and that experts saw it as use of the state machine to boost reelection.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting with concrete fiscal figures and a clear implementation claim.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Bolsonaro's government, though some components depended on Congress and broader fiscal conditions.","contrary_evidence":["Some measures were shaped by Congress and preexisting fiscal rules.","Election-year spending does not prove durable policy success."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Por maioria de votos, TSE declara Bolsonaro inelegível por 8 anos","publisher":"Tribunal Superior Eleitoral","publication_date":"2023-06","url":"https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/noticias/2023/Junho/por-maioria-de-votos-tse-declara-bolsonaro-inelegivel-por-8-anos","claim":"The TSE said Bolsonaro organized the July 2022 ambassadors meeting using the presidency's office and ceremonial structure, public resources, and TV Brasil, as part of a coordinated plan to attack the credibility of electronic voting and influence the electorate.","locator":"decision summary and quoted reasoning in the news release","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official court ruling; retrospective, but directly about a 2022 act and its use of state power.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective but squarely about a 2022 campaign act.","ruler_attribution":"Directly Bolsonaro-specific: the ruling describes his own use of office, public resources, and campaign messaging.","contrary_evidence":["This is a later adjudication of a 2022 act, not a contemporaneous contemporaneous record of intent.","It concerns campaign power use more than routine governing competence."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.5","8B.9","8B.10"]}

Failed directions/blockers: the official TSE candidate/transparency pages were useful for system context, but they did not surface a clean Bolsonaro-specific asset page in the search snippets; Folha direct pages were robots-blocked in this environment, so I relied on UOL/Reuters summaries and TSE rulings instead.
